※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4219 LANG_NAME_IS_THE_COMPILERS

※ A name beginning with `⎕` belongs to the compiler.  A program may read and
※ assign the ones that exist and may not define one, which is what keeps the
※ compiler free to add another without taking a name away from a program
※ written before it existed.

let ⎕tolerance: mut f64 = 1f64

fn ⎕mine() → u8:
    0u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
